			<div class="content" id="post-content-2110746">
									

<p>Many thanks to GottaGoFeast, Oresthin, Fluke, MisterFlames, DrMann, Cimmerian, LordSpy, Zolgamax, and Haecceity in chat for reading this over during the draft stage.</p>
<p>Another tale about an unlisted SCP/anomalous item.</p>
<p>I wrote the majority of this while I was at a small art museum looking at paintings. The premise is essentially that the Foundation, despite having handled the anomalous for so long, still gets things wrong. There will always be things that researchers do not understand, no matter how much they experiment or observe.</p>
<p>Also, pun intended on “slice of life” d:</p>

