					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1404533&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607958888" alt="Zyn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1404533)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;" >Zyn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1411187657 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">20 Sep 2014 04:34</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2114033">
									

<blockquote>
<p>I'll point out that it's very hard to get DNA from hair</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yeah! Hence why the samples had to be sent back to the on-site lab for analysis. Also, since it's hair and not say, saliva or blood that was collected from the tree, it leaves the possibilities open-ended because the DNA analysis likely proved inconclusive (Did the guy become fused with the tree? Or did his mind come to control the tree while his body disappeared? Or is he still alive, but <em>in</em> the tree?)</p>
<p>Much obliged, re: grammar nitpick. I didn't know passerby had a different plural. The more you know&#8230;</p>
<p>Kiryu is a different sort of doctor, I'll grant. I've tried to write him up as a sort of eccentric, wistful individual who enjoys doubling back and thinking about different &quot;what-ifs&quot;. Personal headcanon is the Foundation recruited him from a clinic where he worked as a counselor/therapist. He <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">is made of feels</span> scored high on an EQ test and had a great patient record, etc. etc.</p>
<p>Thanks for the feedback. I really appreciate your attention to detail.</p>
<p><sub>oh and btw fixed your link for you</sub></p>

							</div>

								
